  m_Name: Object_7
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Heat Shield
  description: The Heat Shield, situated at the middle-center-rear of the engine,
    is a small, thin-flat, metal-mid component that protects surrounding parts from
    excessive heat generated by the engine. Its small size and thin shape enable
    it to fit snugly in tight spaces, while its metal-mid material provides sufficient
    heat resistance. Notably, the Heat Shield's position at the rear of the engine
    helps to prevent heat damage to critical components.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
